      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2e069f8fc2c972dd4a0430|full_name}: Thanks for the input, I appreciate it. I can't stress enough how important the \"uncertainty\" aspect of it is so I'm glad you brought it up.\n\nNot knowing whether or not there are jumpscares is where 90% of the anxiety comes from and makes it unbearable to be in worlds that are even /mildly/ unsettling without being absolutely sure, so not even knowing if \"Extreme Horror\" covers that is pretty frustrating. I'd like it to be as on the table as possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-19T22:45:52.412Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I was initially really excited to see that \"Extreme horror\" was a tag in the new content filters, only to be let down by the fact that jumpscares aren't included in this tag.\n\nAs someone with bad anxiety and past trauma from sudden noises and imagery, I'm always really anxious joining spooky worlds not knowing if there'll be jumpscares.\n\nI would really appreciate a tag that clearly states whether or not there will be jumpscares, as I am okay with other types of horror.\n\n(You could maybe argue that this spoils the thrill of the surprise for other people, but I feel like it's not that big of a deal. Not sure where I stand on that yet.)",
